messages.content:
Jordan, before we move to any destructive remediation I propose a recovery plan that first captures a full forensic snapshot: • Freeze the affected payment‑router pods and take memory dumps;
• Export all relevant logs (application, system, audit, network) to immutable storage with timestamps;
• Record a full configuration snapshot of the router service and its dependencies;
• Preserve the current network flow captures for the past 30 minutes.
Once these artifacts are secured and chain‑of‑custody documented, we can proceed with the rollback or patch deployment. I’m requesting approval of this evidence‑preservation‑first recovery plan so we can avoid destroying potential compromise evidence.

